    // gives: overload selection sees the argument BEFORE the declared type adopts it,
    // so an untyped integer literal is still a plain number at a `Double` parameter.
    // It is a chain of SELECTS rather than a chain of blocks on purpose: every
    // operand is already evaluated and every key is a constant, so there is nothing
    // to guard against evaluating, and staying inside one basic block keeps this out
    // of the phi-grouping trap in chapter 4 of the manual.
    function emitPickKey(b, cands, argsV, off, nargs) {
